al responsibility for patient treatment.", "image": "https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/5a3983d88fce9aed3b93c1f0042fe0ca573df746/0_0_5000_4000/master/5000.jpg?width=1200&height=630&quality=85&auto=format&fit=crop&precrop=40:21,offset-x50,offset-y0&overlay-align=bottom%2Cleft&overlay-width=100p&overlay-base64=L2ltZy9zdGF0aWMvb3ZlcmxheXMvdGctZGVmYXVsdC5wbmc&enable=upscale&s=017d0390fab61f85708fa157a1e7e76f", "favicon": "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=theguardian.com&sz=64"}, {"title": "Will AI Replace Healthcare Jobs? Not How You May Think", "source": "Forbes", "url": "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGThexI_9rjHJzsAzzSQmauT8oau5HUByKZz1isMwXidhB2fNQEcQqB58Z62nBVX4Xw0jfYCPcmOarRhiUzrfyojQpJ1htcCuLjAE_z2bEXzoAMFUtoxX79gdJbsQ2PhpflPjHSXoFEAjPRwmP0Cd3cfoAMjF5zffa-UDG5aXPBJFzbkPnraIyLDTbC", "published": "2026-07-03", "summary": "AI is shifting the job market for health professionals away from documentation and medical coding toward roles focused on high-stakes human connection, fine motor skills, and complex decision-making.", "image": "https://imageio.forbes.com/specials-images/imageserve/6a44260badfeba28839f0a92/0x0.jpg?format=jpg&crop=1627,1084,x0,y0,safe&height=900&width=1600&fit=bounds", "favicon": "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=forbes.com&sz=64"}, {"title": "Cedars-Sinai CDAO: Meaningful AI deployment cannot wait", "source": "Becker's Hospital Review", "url": "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFsANs2xxAQPIVGvxvSuyllMK2lMNFdu7uYh7ZY9CBTXRvbMCxGiUScz7VQSxbElFdr1DmXbmHoOpHXBIi9NyrUvmxzs6Gd_RPPky1H8BnKFBteppu_FPhULmTEHlhlYGYS9fIxX7klr5ORT8Dt0tXG5lQgVPUM7NNCe9-DM1I3s6HjfLqwKKy0yi2moGdg_7BMI3KIiDbE4pOBR6LZQL1BVFq0vX63fGSUOrBERw-uFqv469-XZQ==", "published": "2026-06-29", "summary": "Healthcare systems are aggressively deploying AI as a productivity multiplier to help existing clinicians cope with severe labor shortages and reengineer care delivery systems.", "image": null, "favicon": "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=beckershospitalreview.com&sz=64"}]}}, "Arts": {"expires_at": 1784950952.1406422, "feed": {"family": "Arts", "fetched_at": "2026-07-24T21:42:32+00:00", "items": [{"title": "The state of the creative industry 2026: what our survey tells us about pay, burnout and AI", "source": "Creative Boom", "url": "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGrDJh6XXNj537otvJigD56WFbN8Ho3qzGwyvNCQJk0CbwqF_aKSWVizWjxaFuhuuY-Y8jctl-X9Pl6zTMhMABsjdpOoIepUhTBsgKKnwN1crVSDKbYysSB0F2fkWtDs12Eaa9-tbI_vfH2QPLlbzbyOktrUg3x6XvfARFWno9kfsqXEIpJ6e42aLxemXVLqhP78Y6ckPWqQ8hnxl3dygO9cDDdnuCZgwP8oSnQIvJAS801B8Ij7r-1", "published": "2026-06-29", "summary": "A global survey of nearly 900 creative professionals revealed that while 86% of respondents are actively using AI tools in their work, only 10% believe the technology's overall impact on the creative industry is positive, with many reporting increased career anxiety and high rates of burnout.", "image": "https://www.creativeboom.com/upload/articles/ef/efc6ea504d057db7ae8ad00482b2b1b4c4d0ae6a_800.jpeg", "favicon": "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=creativeboom.com&sz=64"}, {"title": "Visual artists are in an AI crisis, this new survey explains why: L.A. arts and culture this weekend", "source": "Los Angeles Times", "url": "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFjZnZ2Mrm96E6cQix3fuLYcDprJymdI3aIvdhWywPIO5JXxDUEesSt8TxSYL9oaFjlv_jyEx2IcTyz2Mgs7bbrOF5AXoEjyn3eM5RURmPBylETBdo4WKRIaNj2Mk_hMN7zrBu-iKBG8LX9fhEYfQyM8bqfvF9DVUdd4aom4bBQphgsV9QWOe9wluKsEDlKQ7zaqk7n4nYpENe7OG2UY47H9NrIicHsmX99X0sNGCty", "published": "2026-05-15", "summary": "Drawing on a landmark Carnegie Mellon University study of verified professional visual artists, this report details how 99% of those surveyed dislike generative AI, voicing critical concerns that employers and clients are driving down human wages by settling for \"good enough\" AI-generated alternatives.", "image": "https://ca-times.brightspotcdn.com/dims4/default/0adb5d1/2147483647/strip/true/crop/4000x2100+0+284/resize/1200x630!/quality/75/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcalifornia-times-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fc7%2F50%2F48a2d631400786682e886a2f0862%2Fopen-ai-98772.jpg", "favicon": "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=latimes.com&sz=64"}, {"title": "AI Won\u2019t Replace Artists", "source": "Forbes", "url": "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHYvz7pD4qPdoILf4VqB9qeBn87xgGvrZbMJkDLqsrWR4kypxQ3ga_D7NlkHuL0Ft20IOtU92d7iSXX8cID5g6jGDzxjOGG5IG0uyZ-tj8jQ7l8nuDF_rmbV8A2OnoYjjsWJ4kT-gnNnSm74j7fFZwhTe9NzdZSrfWSu8UeHM28dnJO7rFV-COQ07uE6p19uSFsxieAVB6EI0Y2ply1qBiP6_-2YC6-L82XnfI=", "published": "2026-05-13", "summary": "This piece analyzes the shifting labor economics of creative careers, arguing that AI has commodified the cheap \"draft layer\" (such as storyboards and concept variations), forcing art graduates to move up the value chain into roles that emphasize high-stakes taste, brand-defining design leadership, and rights assurance.", "image": "https://imageio.forbes.com/specials-images/imageserve/6a035d6372e9b052dc8939be/0x0.jpg?format=jpg&height=900&width=1600&fit=bounds", "favicon": "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=forbes.com&sz=64"}, {"title": "AI Is Changing Creative Work, but the Arts Aren't Disappearing", "source": "Gallup", "url": "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH4_wPcWUkHkFlxe33J2QkYjdByf_g6MBOdqmr0W9h7chZ04gHzLXeTSsC1ZFDcUkdUW7jvy7rwFMPxdy2HwufIywxJvL-gxQtSll0r-PnVUsl7BfJ7uC00UQvV9cingPAIU_HFORWBciWZvW1FHKb2abdNoStufGnzcHLSRZeewJH8tkW4ebyarDWu9u_nB7I4Yd3dVuvaTCo=", "published": "2026-05-03", "summary": "Analyzing national workforce and labor data, this report finds that while generative AI has not yet caused broad declines in artists' overall earnings, it is heavily shifting early-stage creative workflows, with many artists now frequently using AI tools to brainstorm, organize tasks, and quickly experiment with new ideas.", "image": "https://imagekit.gallup.com/fusion/tr:n-emd_soc_meta_og/WORKPLACEV9CMS/243b3f44-365d-4d40-b80f-e91487e4fef0.jpg", "favicon": "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=gallup.com&sz=64"}]}}, "Humanities": {"expires_at": 1784950946.6712, "feed": {"family": "Humanities", "fetched_at": "2026-07-24T21:42:26+00:00", "items": [{"title": "AI, Automation, and the Future of Liberal Arts Degree Careers", "source": "Research.com", "url": "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG93M5G1rOGbIDttjH-OPRhdLU45-gttZhve5PFkH9VSX5VKladfu0isoeGle9-7pF__xwksCY0nBrg-kyjHMikGFnquh51piIZl0Lf_ziN4rjqhKiapyLkax_gbMoBWsJ2N5ZfiQcVqZ8dNa1-FrvuX76WsCvd4WaQjhNeLCI5BONy8MMDCwZX1Mb2D2ou3egK", "published": "2026-07-16", "summary": "This report outlines how the integration of AI is creating hybrid career opportunities for liberal arts graduates, showcasing emerging pathways like \"AI Ethics Specialists\" who combine training in philosophy, law, and social implications to define boundaries for machine-learning systems.", "image": null, "favicon": "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=research.com&sz=64"}, {"title": "Why AI is \u2018resurrecting\u2019 the liberal arts for the Class of 2026", "source": "Wake Forest University News", "url": "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHLRBZqOVx1MhKlVI3xr-Ikh0bwYFTy6aO9hoJN2LR5iDXMfNdyZdrQsIqGuCD2-GdyJTUco-xIytYXOsR1uyitOS0f8wzgzy3BW0GkeCk_07v3C-LREwQKEmme_fbOsqUnA563XlhKk_DBsV_8KA2Mnt_vYN25yIcbhkwYx8YVdqaN_JI7LjlDRHxrlwHuLMGD6akto9b7HkM=", "published": "2026-04-29", "summary": "Career development experts highlight that because AI has commodified execution-level technical tasks, the market is experiencing a reversal in value that highly favors the \"liberal arts brain\" for its emphasis on strategic intent, critical thinking, and ethical oversight.", "image": "https://prod.wp.cdn.aws.wfu.edu/sites/22/2026/04/20260323OPCD80-full.featured.webp", "favicon": "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=news.wfu.edu&sz=64"}, {"title": "AI, Automation, and the Future of Humanities Degree Careers", "source": "Research.com", "url": "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG93M5G1rOGbIDttjH-OPRhdLU45-gttZhve5PFkH9VSX5VKladfu0isoeGle9-7pF__xwksCY0nBrg-kyjHMikGFnquh51piIZl0Lf_ziN4rjqhKiapyLkax_gbMoBWsJ2N5ZfiQcVqZ8dNa1-FrvuX76WsCvd4WaQjhNeLCI5BONy8MMDCwZX1Mb2D2ou3egK", "published": "2026-05-11", "summary": "This analysis explores how AI-driven content automation is shifting employment demands, pushing humanities graduates to adapt by focusing on specialized, high-growth areas like digital humanities and ethical AI development where digital literacy and narrative strategy are prized.", "image": null, "favicon": "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=research.com&sz=64"}, {"title": "Revenge of the Communicators: HR Teams Are Suddenly Scrambling for Good Liberal Arts Talent", "source": "Los Angeles Times", "url": "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEhbOjg1iMNswaQu4UjvZ9Td2F4EHa17GuzZDjoeWJ_8G-b9u1tz2u6VFk4uGYjmX4h0SPR9_H2SWbNSxj0YP5DwEpapg8kSJpkaezYHaZOFSqIUHeXJ341b9K-e0EpL7S6sLEJQwwS7pfxdZ7zz3nwCkQMtCTTFJ_imRZ5PW_1NZjr_9Bqkt3aLUZ17OSm4aI-TLqc2DjEpJLCurk=", "published": "2026-04-19", "summary": "This piece reports on a quiet hiring surge across industries (from tech startups to entertainment giants) that are doubling down on communications and liberal arts majors because of AI's inability to replicate nuanced, human-centric internal storytelling and brand narrative strategies.", "image": "https://ca-times.brightspotcdn.com/dims4/default/b798344/2147483647/strip/true/crop/1366x717+0+96/resize/1200x630!/quality/75/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcalifornia-times-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F03%2Fa4%2F8ab8fbfa40ef953f7344b0db225f%2Fliberal-arts.jpg", "favicon": "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=latimes.com&sz=64"}]}}, "Social sci": {"expires_at": 1784950956.791005, "feed": {"family": "Social sci", "fetched_at": "2026-07-24T21:42:36+00:00", "items": [{"title": "AI Impact on Student Career Choices: Survey Reveals 4 in 10 Rethinking College Majors", "source": "AcademicJobs", "url": "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGrpOpAQFM_q2o9qEyNV7lxpkL6GiaF5XOpF5xBkrzHnHcxCwRG2hNMVC-OicMyddtfQziNMrVXKftucsMumYLm-Pbn16pJmCcSJ7CPfltEA9U3lffphRFlr0Qwo91okkFn9MdN7dgZnX3hpryXGfYNSPlzERdL5meadD6Fdn14DrMywOwoAQ_0Jyk0yjNygeMjlHPROkkqHz8KQ2m2XZ9YnqED7lelcFXl_bUT62HB83suR5rF5g==", "published": "2026-07-23", "summary": "Driven by anxieties over automation, nearly 40% of college students are reconsidering their majors, prompting a significant drop in raw computer science enrollments and a notable shift toward \"AI-resistant\" or hybrid fields that leverage irreplaceable human elements, such as the social sciences, complex problem-solving, and empathy.", "image": null, "favicon": "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=academicjobs.com&sz=64"}, {"title": "AI, Automation, and the Future of Sociology and Political Science Careers", "source": "Research.com", "url": "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEYC8CBA2rq4epqQHX5kk7r6DcqfpPF82rAT8Gs585jEyXbkrGfGPf6V9jUu_fTvU0iuach8l2-pmSE3tuHLIT3XQAOsuVfC3JJxQa68Jc038Auimiu4PLulpn3lZpmOANpkDFxfZKAjukoCOkgjtM3W4YgHUviTQSTTgwNtl9-gr3LANFxL8mpYINuhSCfPA==", "published": "2026-07-16", "summary": "While basic data entry and routine reporting in the social sciences face high automation risks, overall hiring for social researchers with AI expertise is projected to rise 15% over the next decade as roughly 45% of political and sociological roles now require proficiency in AI-assisted data interpretation.", "image": null, "favicon": "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=research.com&sz=64"}, {"title": "AI and the Labor Market: Revolution or Evolution?", "source": "Encoura", "url": "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGU7qoEV8DYQs9iOl23I0aoH1ZjClffjS4J5QEBRWDpa2a1icP5F_nKuMU8ZTTOo7yJpUVS4g34t7UYCoy0gDepOX4jNIPI5aSKNZjKJyzj8wUpr2FMIgLwONa3Vdo79_1GXZqoMxhe17b1Awwt1Tbhe29lkIKBO9cYYz7j2LAqZrAtuKd5Rdv82D4BEeeMJPiMdWhJNu0xBolU", "published": "2026-07-13", "summary": "This labor market analysis reveals that fields like the humanities and social sciences\u2014which prioritize interpretation, ethics, and human context\u2014are highly resilient, though social science graduates are strongly encouraged to pick up complementary tech skills to qualify for the surging number of \"AI-ready\" job postings.", "image": "https://cdn.builder.io/api/v1/image/assets%2Fd8f241c150da4717b19490064ab73cc5%2F4c5f873a25584083b78ad075e2d979cf", "favicon": "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=encoura.org&sz=64"}, {"title": "GovAI Opportunities 2026: Apply for Research, AI Policy, Chief of Staff and Operations Roles with Salaries Up to $205,000", "source": "Opportunities for Youth", "url": "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE9doZnU9CSqymPgGNn3GqV4Uji34X3iS0qvk_pWAVOyJu6QbxbpYOQPgS2JTrAkoSpn9Bag3l-9Vt2hXFyiS0swWe_5YybodETbnCp6XatnbbDFt_bU3WHMReNVguMcLxg9NMVyK_MuS9rWdBEOdr3CGIi9hmCVbB_cGdGY6Oq_SDKioJZqFt8SZh9AgbvUlkNOpXAYshwP96KRY2r-qt2lUAx7d4DGxxpr2LJ8O_vz-Qgze2_e5amHkLA7zu3oNzVdw33DPOjhmHsDJRAhMK0l30geVJ3vSqjcerB_-E=", "published": "2026-07-24", "summary": "The rapid deployment of advanced machine learning models is creating high-paying, non-technical jobs in AI governance, safety, and regulation (with salaries up to $205,000), actively recruiting social science backgrounds to tackle geopolitical risks, ethical guidelines, and public policy frameworks.", "image": "https://i0.wp.com/opportunitiesforyouth.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Screenshot_20260724-144653-display-0.png.png", "favicon": "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=opportunitiesforyouth.org&sz=64"}]}}, "STEM": {"expires_at": 1784950948.6617758, "feed": {"family": "STEM", "fetched_at": "2026-07-24T21:42:28+00:00", "items": [{"title": "College graduates face competitive market as artificial intelligence spending rises", "source": "Fox 13 News", "url": "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG2pY-ELbz5pOM6egB7uh9j2g1uwGg0J6Fb86mrTO0HYj2uSOJneAb71AZVCCfzQpny3mi40MOATipI2diWXiwuJehUvE3wHVr0sNO1QvfTjL6jijZmi7ORSNJiN76goHkmy0pj_-yyhe1aMq14bMRNQMajGMp8XiJrMnIxr2aC8jayuyy792b0Aj2Fk9_GFIkrIQ6_-3zlkybSSGmq4fQOhHUWf80LFNnSig==", "published": "2026-07-24", "summary": "A new survey highlights a tightening entry-level market, showing that nearly half of hiring managers are choosing to redirect recruitment funds to invest in AI tools rather than train new graduates, meaning STEM applicants must demonstrate immediate technical competency and strong soft skills to get hired.", "image": "https://images.foxtv.com/static.fox13news.com/www.fox13news.com/content/uploads/2023/07/1200/630/GettyImages-1247553442.jpg?ve=1&tl=1", "favicon": "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=fox13news.com&sz=64"}, {"title": "Top\u00a0STEM Jobs for\u00a0AI\u00a0Career Advancement", "source": "Capitol Technology University", "url": "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHicsZZvQKV4j8OQu9WU18STDXAaxylot03hDpX3U0VhF3PYljhQXX9D2oKL1FUf_gzvlCu3pw0Ct9FzTAA-k4lXmU4gtqB5j0K9iRyVcFRgWXRtYmjSI2jDC8lvogwXS-HViGpt8TXs4_FGpXa3zddRofJFfdln8HIrLsy", "published": "2026-07-11", "summary": "While 88% of organizations have integrated AI, a severe skills gap persists, offering high-paying premiums for STEM grads who can master AI/ML, data science, and \"AI workflow specialist\" roles that connect intelligent systems to business operations.", "image": "https://www.captechu.edu/sites/default/files/AI%20Careers%20Blog.png", "favicon": "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=captechu.edu&sz=64"}, {"title": "What types of AI jobs are emerging for new college graduates?", "source": "Research.com", "url": "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQErWeDQNQJ6aiva2pHMM61vy6qDpycdOh5fdbK3SHQcObhpmWATF4QE8KtAjFVy739xbizhoGzmmJY9knX5shPZnwB1Pzg3mYUHyc0QUHgUCQtxBTy-k60Ikzvww4Rkq1Mm6KLbRUedW0NyCkhb_d5krqs-7TVvyheXNMxMlzNWkMw0LRCaaer3Rn7cMsIsRrjg4fBGaGPWpEmBpVp44Fea41s=", "published": "2026-07-09", "summary": "This report outlines that 35% of all entry-level job postings now specifically require AI-related skills, fueling demand for STEM majors in emerging pathways like AI data curation, AI ethics, and ethical AI development.", "image": null, "favicon": "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=research.com&sz=64"}, {"title": "Class of 2026: Young college graduates and AI-exposed occupations", "source": "Economic Policy Institute (EPI)", "url": "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHeYWXRm90Xjvdr_a1yKSm-uj907SmapeA9ob-5iJxaatz18AEgpXKH9EMXWp-hmZKpO8G1Pya8nPpAuAlzkMesBOe0zjyCAOGdS-ZH8sMWXEShsSvEkv2yskxxy2LCwd_GgHLld09aR7MwexrsGWzE8XiDB12W4uUMaW6fyq2ayh4cNol5tHF04hJFvT8usDFXMsUaoVIxjiNYJH20E9XGAkLX3olJKtrTMbcF_Zg=", "published": "2026-05-21", "summary": "Data analyzing the newest graduating class indicates that although STEM majors are highly exposed to AI tools in their daily careers, this exposure is not driving a displacement of young tech workers but is instead requiring them to act as the direct operators of AI systems.", "image": null, "favicon": "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=epi.org&sz=64"}]}}, "Other": {"expires_at": 1784951008.028901, "feed": {"family": "Other", "fetched_at": "2026-07-24T21:43:28+00:00", "items": [{"title": "Why the liberal arts can help young Americans prepare for the era of AI", "source": "CBS News", "url": "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHGIfogsD88tFqyzMWtkaS6CItmgcclCa3DYXpRdTXV1YSIom7sXZ74XpKzrHz8MQenQRaj2acRb_X2u4WgXtx6K9Hgzy9hRIB1jot4PvsLNNq2rSKJH5s_mxDLA9K-4zaLbCiT7cgfu7TUx1oVBndx_Hvw4gLdyhkI0ndNPb8r2H9L_e79t-M=", "published": "2026-06-12", "summary": "Career experts suggest that as AI automates hig