cting the labor market toward highly secure, well-paying trade roles requiring physical dexterity and manual problem-solving.", "image": null, "favicon": "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=bvwd.ca.gov&sz=64"}, {"title": "AI Blue-Collar Job Shift", "source": "Traube Tent (featuring CNBC market analysis)", "url": "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGPDjHkbz5Fb4nEMJfduOXCqCLubTGYDP_KvhtRNg2CLw13Bu84QV96JZxcTAd8CEgrZ9eWqaT1GqeW0YfhPr7fnWF8FGmLWuMNj0AVza-YaHKQYRI2uAX031PmQH_V61SfPvbd-n6eXMBshX89zs5xK6vj_LHYrYYc0qWhAeNgK44BPG8R0U9dKN81TtThyaa_Hv7DkAm4oRSsfqnY_JqgUvLZozpum5Nh0asWBXRgi7ZC", "published": "2026-06-18", "summary": "Major industrial and telecom employers like Ford and AT&T are ramping up recruitment of trade majors\u2014including mechanics, technicians, and electricians\u2014to support hardware-heavy initiatives like 5G rollouts and electric vehicle manufacturing that are immune to AI automation.", "image": null, "favicon": "https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=traubetent.com&sz=64"}]}}}
